{
  "children": [
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Al-doped LiNi₀.₈Mn₀.₁Co₀.₁O₂ cathodes with improved cycling stability at 4.4 V",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Title"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "L. Volta, M. Faraday, N. Nernst",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Author"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Ni-rich layered oxides offer high capacity but suffer from capacity fade above 4.3 V. We show that 1 mol % Al doping of NMC811 raises capacity retention after 300 cycles at 1C from 71 % to 89 %, and reduces the charge-transfer resistance growth by a factor of three. Galvanostatic intermittent titration shows that Li⁺ diffusion is unaffected by doping.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Abstract"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "lithium-ion battery · NMC811 · doping · impedance · GITT",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Keywords"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Introduction",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The energy density of a cell scales with the product of specific capacity and average voltage,",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "E = \\int_0^{Q} V(q)\\,dq \\approx Q\\,\\bar V,",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:energy",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "which motivates Ni-rich cathodes ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "manthiram2020"
          ],
          "style": "cite",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Experimental",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Co-precipitation of Ni₀.₈Mn₀.₁Co₀.₁(OH)₂, Al(NO₃)₃ added to 1 mol %",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Lithiation with LiOH·H₂O (5 % excess), 750 °C, 12 h, O₂ flow",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Electrodes: 90:5:5 active:C65:PVDF, 10 mg/cm²",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "CR2032 half-cells vs Li, 1 M LiPF₆ in EC:EMC 3:7",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        }
      ],
      "type": "List"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Results and discussion",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Cycling",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "rows": [
        [
          "Sample",
          "Q₁ at 0.1C (mAh/g)",
          "ICE (\\%)",
          "Q at 5C (mAh/g)",
          "Retention 300 cyc (\\%)"
        ],
        [
          "NMC811",
          "214",
          "88.1",
          "142",
          "71.2"
        ],
        [
          "Al-NMC811",
          "209",
          "89.4",
          "151",
          "89.0"
        ]
      ],
      "caption": "Electrochemical performance, 2.8–4.4 V.",
      "label": "tab:cycle",
      "alignment": "lrrrr",
      "style": "booktabs",
      "type": "Table"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Impedance",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nyquist spectra were fitted to a Randles circuit with Warburg element:",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "Z(\\omega) = R_s + \\frac{R_{ct} + Z_W}{1 + j\\omega C_{dl}(R_{ct}+Z_W)},\\qquad Z_W = \\frac{\\sigma_W}{\\sqrt\\omega}(1-j).",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:randles",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "After 300 cycles ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "R_{ct}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " grew from 18 to 142 Ω for undoped and from 16 to 54 Ω for doped material.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Diffusion",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "From GITT, the chemical diffusion coefficient is ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "weppner1977"
          ],
          "style": "cite",
          "type": "Citation"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "\\tilde D = \\frac{4}{\\pi\\tau}\\left(\\frac{m_B V_M}{M_B S}\\right)^2\\left(\\frac{\\Delta E_s}{\\Delta E_\\tau}\\right)^2,",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:gitt",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "yielding ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\tilde D \\sim 10^{-10}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " cm²/s for both materials at 50 % state of charge.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Thermodynamics",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The open-circuit voltage relates to the Gibbs energy via ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\Delta G = -nFE",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and its temperature coefficient gives the entropic heat:",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "\\Delta S = nF\\left(\\frac{\\partial E}{\\partial T}\\right)_p.",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:entropy",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Conclusions",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Al doping suppresses the H2→H3 phase transition and surface reconstruction, giving 89 % retention at 4.4 V without compromising rate capability.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
